AU](https://zimmermann-sit.sfdc-8tgtt5-ecom1.exp-delivery.com/) | [SITUS](https://zimmermann-sit.sfdc-8tgtt5-ecom1.exp-delivery.com/us/) | [SITUK](https://zimmermann-sit.sfdc-8tgtt5-ecom1.exp-delivery.com/uk/) | [SITEU-E](https://zimmermann-sit.sfdc-8tgtt5-ecom1.exp-delivery.com/en-eu/) | [SITEU-F](https://zimmermann-sit.sfdc-8tgtt5-ecom1.exp-delivery.com/fr-eu/) | [SITEU-I](https://zimmermann-sit.sfdc-8tgtt5-ecom1.exp-delivery.com/it-eu/) | [SITEU-S](https://zimmermann-sit.sfdc-8tgtt5-ecom1.exp-delivery.com/es-eu/) | [SITEU-INTL](https://zimmermann-sit.sfdc-8tgtt5-ecom1.exp-delivery.com/en-ch/) | [SITHK](https://zimmermann-sit.sfdc-8tgtt5-ecom1.exp-delivery.com/hk/) | [SITME](https://zimmermann-sit.sfdc-8tgtt5-ecom1.exp-delivery.com/en-ae/) | SITUS-INTL |\n| UAT |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n\nSIT — Operational Details\n-------------------------\n\nSIT is a dedicated MRT environment for NewStore order management integration testing. It receives the same build as Digital Dev but points to a separate SFCC instance and has third-party integrations disabled (Einstein, Global-e, Narvar).\n\nIt is a **parallel lane** — it never gates the Digital release path. Digital Dev can proceed to release regardless of SIT status. The two lanes converge only at **STAGE**, where both Digital Dev green and NewStore OMS SIT complete are required before promotion. See the Environment Topology & Promotion Path page for the full six-tier model.\n\n### Deployment\n\n| Who deploys | How | When |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| CI (GitHub Actions) | Automatic | After `sit-gate` passes on every `develop` push |\n| Developer | Manual via `npm run push:sit && npm run activate:sit` | For hotfixes or out-of-band testing |\n\nManual deployments must use a `sit/*` or `hotfix/*` branch. Never push to SIT from `develop` or `main` without the CI gate having first confirmed Digital Dev is green.\n\n### CI tagging\n\nEvery SIT deployment creates a `sit/deploy/{YYYY-MM-DD}-{sha}` git tag — NewStore uses this as the bundle reference when triaging integration failures. Sprint boundary tags (`sprint/{N}/{YYYY-MM-DD}`) are created automatically when `scripts/sprint.txt` is updated on a `develop` push.\n\n### Critical rules\n\n* **Never** direct production or UAT traffic to SIT.\n* **Never** enable Einstein, Global-e, or Narvar on SIT — see `config/sit.js`.\n* **Never** use SIT as a hotfix path to PROD. Hotfixes follow `hotfix/* → main → PROD`.\n* If SIT is broken, **do not block** the Digital release — raise with the NewStore team independently.\n* SIT SFCC credentials (`COMMERCE_API_*_SIT`) are separate from Digital Dev credentials — changing one set does not affect the other.\n\n### Config\n\nThe environment override is at `config/sit.js`. It reads four environment variables set as GitHub Secrets: `COMMERCE_API_CLIENT_ID_SIT`, `COMMERCE_API_ORG_ID_SIT`, `COMMERCE_API_SHORT_CODE_SIT`, `COMMERCE_API_SITE_ID_SIT`. MRT push credentials (`MRT_USER`, `MRT_API_KEY`) are shared with Digital Dev and scoped to the project slug in `mobify.config.js`.\n\n### Rollback\n\nIf SIT serves a bad build, in order of speed:\n\n1. **MRT Console rollback** — fastest: activate the previous bundle via the MRT Console UI. Previous bundle IDs are visible on the SIT environment page.\n2. **Git tag revert** — identify the last good `sit/deploy/*` tag, check out that SHA, and run `npm run push:sit && npm run activate:sit` manually.\n3. **CI re-run** — re-run the last successful `digital-sit.yml` workflow run that deployed a known-good build.\n\nOption 1 is preferred. Contact the Integration Lead (#integration) if MRT Console access is needed in an emergency.\n\n### Contact\n\n| Situation | Contact | Channel |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| SIT SFCC credentials | Integration Lead | #integration |\n| NewStore SIT testing status | NewStore delivery team | (project delivery channel) |\n| MRT SIT environment issues | Accenture DevOps | #integration |\n| SIT blocking a release | Integration Lead + both squad leads | #dev-team |",
      "format": "markdown"
